Well. I see lot of players  criticize this game for having an automated battle but I don't see this as a big problem since the game actualy offers good options in deck preparation which could change the outcome of the battle. In this the game is quite interesting and engaging, and I actually ike it a lot.
Pros:
- Easy to grasp game mechanics;
- Big variety of skills;
- A lot of upgrades (great sense of progression);
- Many options of fights to pick;
- Nice setting;
- Could be played for free;
Cons:
- Time consuming - even if you pay it is hard to escape the grind and time waiting (except if you pay a lot);
- Cearly deigned for mobiles and then switched to PC (it messes up with the above mentioned time consumption);
Generally I would recommend the game to anyone who likes progression games and light strategy of deck buildings as well as all the fans of Lovecraftian settings (although there is only setting - no real, engaging story in the game).

